    "headline": "Off Boys owns the week, while four teams crowd the top at 4-1",
    "deck": "Off Boys posted a Week 5-best 145.90, Sullco MethMouths climbed into the 4-1 pack, and the player leaderboard helps explain the week’s biggest swings without replacing the official GFL team totals.",
    "story": [
      "Off Boys delivered the top GFL score of Week 5 at 145.90 and beat THE Barton Spartans by 23.94. That moved Off Boys to 3-2, not undefeated, and gave the club three straight wins after an 0-2 start.",
      "The standings now feature four teams at 4-1: Sullco MethMouths, Redwood Murder, Eskimo Brothers, and California Un-Named Team. Their paths differ. Sullco led the four in points through five weeks at 612.56, while California Un-Named Team remains 4-1 despite a Week 5 loss to Your Mom.",
      "Player factors added useful context this week. Drake Maye topped the pasted ESPN Week 5 leaderboard at 39.46 for Sullco MethMouths, while Off Boys had four listed players at 16.00 or better, led by Jahmyr Gibbs at 35.20 and Puka Nacua at 29.20.",
      "Medford MountainMen also placed six players in the pasted top 50, including Christian Watson at 29.30 and Parker Washington at 27.40. The team scored 105.32 and earned its first win, showing why individual leaderboard strength should be treated as context rather than a substitute for final lineup totals."
    ],
